# {{TITLE}}: lessons from videos

The user sends videos about {{TOPIC}} to learn from. This skill is the memory
of what they taught, so it carries across every chat. It was built by the
learn-from-video skill; keep it current with the procedure at the bottom.

## What is in here

- `references/principles.md`: the rulebook. Every lesson with its sources,
  the exact numbers the creators gave (with timestamps), and which videos
  added it, agreed with it or disagreed. Read it before giving advice that
  depends on a detail.
- `references/video-index.md`: every video studied, one line each: who,
  how long, how it was studied, what it is good for. Start here to find a
  source.
- `references/videos/<id>.md`: detailed notes per video, with timestamps
  and a "What's on screen" section when frames were studied.
- `references/transcripts/<id>.txt`: the transcripts the notes were built
  from, with [mm:ss] marks. Search these when the notes don't answer a
  question.

## The lessons in one page

Ordered by how much they matter. "(n/N videos)" is how many of the N videos
studied so far taught it. Numbers are the creators' own; **(inference)**
marks anything worked out here rather than said in a video.

_No videos studied yet._

