## When a new video arrives

Study it with the learn-from-video skill (it uses /watch for the transcript
and frames), then keep this skill current, because that is the point of it.
If the video is about a different topic, it belongs in another
`*-video-lessons` skill instead (or as well).

1. Save the transcript to `references/transcripts/<id>.txt` and write
   `references/videos/<id>.md` in the same format as the others.
2. Add a row to `references/video-index.md`.
3. Mark each lesson NEW, AGREES or CONFLICTS against
   `references/principles.md`; update the rulebook, then the one-page list
   above (bump every "(n/N videos)" count, since N grows for all of them).
4. Never invent numbers; mark guesses **(inference)**. Skip sponsor reads,
   app click-paths and motivation.
5. Tell the user in a few plain lines what was new and what it changes.
